Per-resource intents (E24b) in the broker; gate the E24 intent attacks

An intent binds a tool and, optionally, named arguments
(write_file path=/workspace/reports/a.md; a rename's source and
destination). Matching is E24b's rule; the check stores the matched
intent and, under the same lock, the effect path consumes exactly that
one; the audit record names it. Loading fails closed (a constraint
without '=', an empty name or value, a repeated name, a path not in
normal form) and orders intents broadest first, the order E24b's
broadest_listed_first_is_consumed assumes. Tool-only intents files work
unchanged.

tests/intents_resource.py, predictions first, 13/13: binding, once
only, another file refused, tool-only as before, attenuation (an intent
for a delete the policy forbids is refused by the policy and kept),
load order, a rename intent binding both paths, malformed intents
refused.

tests/intent_attacks.py (the original E24 attacks) needs a running
broker and was in no workflow, so it had never been gated.
tests/run_intent_attacks.sh starts one the way the test expects
(6/6) and now runs in CI.

